# US House — 1, 2, 3, 4

## Founding paragraph

The US House is a software-house organization for turning an idea into a traceable, usable result: **1 Origin, 2 Custody, 3 Production, 4 Release**. The order is the central improvement: every program action should have a beginning, a controlled state, an actual production record, and a separately identifiable release state. Convenience is added without losing provenance, and software operations such as installation, deletion, update, repair, and deployment remain attributable and reviewable.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    O["1 — Origin\nIdea / Request / Source"] --> C["2 — Custody\nHold / Control / Version"]
    C --> P["3 — Production\nBuild / Execute / Install / Update / Remove"]
    P --> R["4 — Release\nDeploy / Deliver / Verify"]
    R --> N["Next revision / next Origin"]

    P --> W["Windows\nPowerShell / CMD"]
    P --> U["Ubuntu / Linux\nShell"]
    P --> MS["Microsoft software\npackage lifecycle"]
    P --> AP["Apple software\npackage lifecycle"]

    O -.-> E["Evidence"]
    C -.-> E
    P -.-> E
    R -.-> E
```

## The four documents

| Order | Document | Meaning | Typical evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Origin | Why and from where | request, source, proposal |
| 2 | Custody | Where and under whose control | repository, package, version, hash |
| 3 | Production | What actually happened | command, build, install, update, remove, test |
| 4 | Release | What became available | artifact, deployment, verification |

## Improvement rule

The system improves by adding precision without breaking the order. A convenience command is still a production event; an installation is still production; a deletion is still production; an update creates a new state; and a release is not assumed merely because production succeeded.

## Evidence rule

Every important operation SHOULD be representable as:

`origin → custody → production → release → verification`

Unknown information remains explicitly unknown. A proposition remains a proposition until supported by an appropriate source or verification record.

## Software-house scope

The US House software layer can organize:

- Windows installation, update, removal, repair, and status operations.
- Ubuntu/Linux equivalents.
- Microsoft and Apple software catalog entries.
- Convenience menus and command wrappers.
- Source/build/deployment tracking.
- Evidence and integrity records.

Vendor inclusion is a technical catalog decision and does not imply endorsement, ownership, or governmental affiliation.

## Relationship to .hsss

The companion `.hsss` document is the hierarchical specification. This `.mmd` document is the visual/order document. The `.hsss` explains the system; the `.mmd` makes its four-stage structure directly renderable.
